  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The data management team has not finished the export for this project, and I cannot infer the number of measured features from its working filename. There are two plausible releases: a compact targeted panel and a large untargeted panel. Both releases have the same participants and would otherwise satisfy the paired-table requirements. Our funding milestone requires retaining every pair of features and every participant in a single run. Reducing the panel, dropping people, or splitting the requested output into multiple independent runs has not been approved. I need a capability judgment that waits for the size fact rather than assuming the smaller release. Can LIONESS-DRAGON process all feature pairs for our 100 participants? There are either 100 or 1000 total features across the two layers; the export manifest has not arrived."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Routing matched these registered workflows to your words, but the capability check did not confirm that any of them gives what you asked for:\n- **LIONESS-DRAGON** — produces: One two-layer partial-correlation network per sample, plus the aggregate.\n- **DRAGON** — produces: One undirected partial-correlation network within and between two matched omics layers (any two, e.g. expression and methylation), across all samples. A p-value and a Benjamini-Hochberg adjusted p-value for every edge (adjusted within each layer and across the layers), to filter edges by significance.\n\nCompare what each produces with what you asked for. Ask again to re-run the check, or say which result you want and from which workflow.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
